# LOCAL-FIRST (2026-08-19): never bake a database into the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY server/ ./`, and since the SQLite switch there is
# now a real database sitting at server/prisma/dev.db on any machine that has
# run the app. Without these lines, your laptop's test database — test
# customers, test sales — gets copied into every image built and shipped to
# every site. It wouldn't even be used (the live one lives at /data/prod.db),
# it would just be stowaway data riding along, in an image that gets pushed
# around and kept.
#
# Same list as server/.gitignore, for the same reason: this file is DATA and
# belongs in exactly one place, on the box that owns it.
*.db
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
